{"document":{"type":"root","children":[{"type":"code","value":"function useAsyncDebouncedCallback<TFn>(fn, options): (...args) => Promise<Awaited<ReturnType<TFn>> | undefined>;","lang":"ts"},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Defined in: "},{"type":"link","href":"https://github.com/TanStack/pacer/blob/main/packages/react-pacer/src/async-debouncer/useAsyncDebouncedCallback.ts#L46","children":[{"type":"text","value":"async-debouncer/useAsyncDebouncedCallback.ts:46"}]}]},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"A React hook that creates a debounced version of an async callback function.\nThis hook is a convenient wrapper around the "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"useAsyncDebouncer"},{"type":"text","value":" hook,\nproviding a stable, debounced async function reference for use in React components."}]},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"The debounced async function will only execute after the specified wait time has elapsed\nsince its last invocation. If called again before the wait time expires, the timer\nresets and starts waiting again. The returned function always returns a promise. The call\nthat triggers an execution resolves or rejects with that execution's result; superseded\ncalls resolve with the most recent result (which may be "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"undefined"},{"type":"text","value":" if nothing has executed\nyet), and calls made while the debouncer is disabled resolve with "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"undefined"},{"type":"text","value":"."}]},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"This hook provides a simpler API compared to "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"useAsyncDebouncer"},{"type":"text","value":", making it ideal for basic\nasync debouncing needs. However, it does not expose the underlying AsyncDebouncer instance."}]},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"For advanced usage requiring features like:"}]},{"type":"list","ordered":false,"items":[{"type":"listItem","children":[{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Manual cancellation"}]}]},{"type":"listItem","children":[{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Access to execution/error state"}]}]},{"type":"listItem","children":[{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Custom useCallback dependencies"}]}]}]},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Consider using the "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"useAsyncDebouncer"},{"type":"text","value":" hook instead."}]},{"type":"heading","depth":2,"id":"type-parameters","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Type Parameters"}]},{"type":"heading","depth":3,"id":"tfn","children":[{"type":"text","value":"TFn"}]},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"inlineCode","value":"TFn"},{"type":"text","value":" "},{"type":"emphasis","children":[{"type":"text","value":"extends"}]},{"type":"text","value":" "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"AnyAsyncFunction"}]},{"type":"heading","depth":2,"id":"parameters","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Parameters"}]},{"type":"heading","depth":3,"id":"fn","children":[{"type":"text","value":"fn"}]},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"inlineCode","value":"TFn"}]},{"type":"heading","depth":3,"id":"options","children":[{"type":"text","value":"options"}]},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"link","href":"../interfaces/ReactAsyncDebouncerOptions.md","children":[{"type":"inlineCode","value":"ReactAsyncDebouncerOptions"}]},{"type":"text","value":"<"},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"TFn"},{"type":"text","value":", {\n}>"}]},{"type":"heading","depth":2,"id":"returns","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Returns"}]},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"(..."},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"args"},{"type":"text","value":") => "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"Promise"},{"type":"text","value":"<"},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"Awaited"},{"type":"text","value":"<"},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"ReturnType"},{"type":"text","value":"<"},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"TFn"},{"type":"text","value":">> | "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"undefined"},{"type":"text","value":">"}]},{"type":"heading","depth":2,"id":"example","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Example"}]},{"type":"code","value":"// Debounce an async search handler\nconst handleSearch = useAsyncDebouncedCallback(async (query: string) => {\n  const results = await fetchSearchResults(query);\n  return results;\n}, {\n  wait: 500 // Wait 500ms between executions\n});\n\n// Use in an input\n<input\n  type=\"search\"\n  onChange={e => handleSearch(e.target.value)}\n/>","lang":"tsx"}],"headings":[{"id":"type-parameters","text":"Type Parameters","level":2},{"id":"tfn","text":"TFn","level":3},{"id":"parameters","text":"Parameters","level":2},{"id":"fn","text":"fn","level":3},{"id":"options","text":"options","level":3},{"id":"returns","text":"Returns","level":2},{"id":"example","text":"Example","level":2}]},"frameworks":[],"downloadMarkdown":"\n```ts\nfunction useAsyncDebouncedCallback<TFn>(fn, options): (...args) => Promise<Awaited<ReturnType<TFn>> | undefined>;\n```\n\nDefined in: [async-debouncer/useAsyncDebouncedCallback.ts:46](https://github.com/TanStack/pacer/blob/main/packages/react-pacer/src/async-debouncer/useAsyncDebouncedCallback.ts#L46)\n\nA React hook that creates a debounced version of an async callback function.\nThis hook is a convenient wrapper around the `useAsyncDebouncer` hook,\nproviding a stable, debounced async function reference for use in React components.\n\nThe debounced async function will only execute after the specified wait time has elapsed\nsince its last invocation. If called again before the wait time expires, the timer\nresets and starts waiting again. The returned function always returns a promise. The call\nthat triggers an execution resolves or rejects with that execution's result; superseded\ncalls resolve with the most recent result (which may be `undefined` if nothing has executed\nyet), and calls made while the debouncer is disabled resolve with `undefined`.\n\nThis hook provides a simpler API compared to `useAsyncDebouncer`, making it ideal for basic\nasync debouncing needs. However, it does not expose the underlying AsyncDebouncer instance.\n\nFor advanced usage requiring features like:\n- Manual cancellation\n- Access to execution/error state\n- Custom useCallback dependencies\n\nConsider using the `useAsyncDebouncer` hook instead.\n\n## Type Parameters\n\n### TFn\n\n`TFn` *extends* `AnyAsyncFunction`\n\n## Parameters\n\n### fn\n\n`TFn`\n\n### options\n\n[`ReactAsyncDebouncerOptions`](../interfaces/ReactAsyncDebouncerOptions.md)\\<`TFn`, \\{\n\\}\\>\n\n## Returns\n\n(...`args`) => `Promise`\\<`Awaited`\\<`ReturnType`\\<`TFn`\\>\\> \\| `undefined`\\>\n\n## Example\n\n```tsx\n// Debounce an async search handler\nconst handleSearch = useAsyncDebouncedCallback(async (query: string) => {\n  const results = await fetchSearchResults(query);\n  return results;\n}, {\n  wait: 500 // Wait 500ms between executions\n});\n\n// Use in an input\n<input\n  type=\"search\"\n  onChange={e => handleSearch(e.target.value)}\n/>\n```\n","originalRawMarkdown":"---\nid: useAsyncDebouncedCallback\ntitle: useAsyncDebouncedCallback\n---\n\n```ts\nfunction useAsyncDebouncedCallback<TFn>(fn, options): (...args) => Promise<Awaited<ReturnType<TFn>> | undefined>;\n```\n\nDefined in: [async-debouncer/useAsyncDebouncedCallback.ts:46](https://github.com/TanStack/pacer/blob/main/packages/react-pacer/src/async-debouncer/useAsyncDebouncedCallback.ts#L46)\n\nA React hook that creates a debounced version of an async callback function.\nThis hook is a convenient wrapper around the `useAsyncDebouncer` hook,\nproviding a stable, debounced async function reference for use in React components.\n\nThe debounced async function will only execute after the specified wait time has elapsed\nsince its last invocation. If called again before the wait time expires, the timer\nresets and starts waiting again. The returned function always returns a promise. The call\nthat triggers an execution resolves or rejects with that execution's result; superseded\ncalls resolve with the most recent result (which may be `undefined` if nothing has executed\nyet), and calls made while the debouncer is disabled resolve with `undefined`.\n\nThis hook provides a simpler API compared to `useAsyncDebouncer`, making it ideal for basic\nasync debouncing needs. However, it does not expose the underlying AsyncDebouncer instance.\n\nFor advanced usage requiring features like:\n- Manual cancellation\n- Access to execution/error state\n- Custom useCallback dependencies\n\nConsider using the `useAsyncDebouncer` hook instead.\n\n## Type Parameters\n\n### TFn\n\n`TFn` *extends* `AnyAsyncFunction`\n\n## Parameters\n\n### fn\n\n`TFn`\n\n### options\n\n[`ReactAsyncDebouncerOptions`](../interfaces/ReactAsyncDebouncerOptions.md)\\<`TFn`, \\{\n\\}\\>\n\n## Returns\n\n(...`args`) => `Promise`\\<`Awaited`\\<`ReturnType`\\<`TFn`\\>\\> \\| `undefined`\\>\n\n## Example\n\n```tsx\n// Debounce an async search handler\nconst handleSearch = useAsyncDebouncedCallback(async (query: string) => {\n  const results = await fetchSearchResults(query);\n  return results;\n}, {\n  wait: 500 // Wait 500ms between executions\n});\n\n// Use in an input\n<input\n  type=\"search\"\n  onChange={e => handleSearch(e.target.value)}\n/>\n```\n"}
